  "issue": {
    "id": "I_kwDOAd1its8AAAABBsmHLQ",
    "databaseId": 4408837933,
    "number": 1838,
    "title": "[Lyrical T&T] 404 Not Found during Debian Install on Ubuntu 26.04 (AMD64)",
    "url": "https://github.com/ros2/ros2/issues/1838",
    "body": "### Generated by Generative AI\n\nWhile attempting to install `ros-lyrical-desktop` on a fresh Ubuntu 26.04 (Resolute) Docker container, the process fails at the end of the download with multiple 404 errors.\n\n### Operating System:\n\n OS : Ubuntu 26.04 (Docker) Arch: amd64 (Intel i7-13700HX) > Repository:http://packages.ros.org/ros2-testing/ubuntu\n\n### ROS version or commit hash:\n\nROS 2 Lyrical Luth\n\n### RMW implementation (if applicable):\n\nrmw_fastrtps_cpp\n\n### RMW Configuration (if applicable):\n\nDefault\n\n### Client library (if applicable):\n\ninsatllation issue\n\n### 'ros2 doctor --report' output\n\n\n\"Cannot run; installation failed to complete.\"\n\n### Steps to reproduce issue\n\n1.Start ubuntu:26.04 Docker container.\n\n2.Add ros2-testing repository.\n\n3.Run apt update.\n\n4.Run apt install ros-lyrical-desktop -y.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nhe packages should download and install successfully\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nhe process stopped at 99% with multiple '404 Not Found' errors for specific .deb files.\n\n### Additional information\n\nam participating in the Lyrical Luth T&T Party. I am testing on a Lenovo LOQ laptop using Docker. It appears the mirrors are not fully synced for the resolute (26.04) distribution.\"",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Generated by Generative AI</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">While attempting to install <code class=\"notranslate\">ros-lyrical-desktop</code> on a fresh Ubuntu 26.04 (Resolute) Docker container, the process fails at the end of the download with multiple 404 errors.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Operating System:</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">OS : Ubuntu 26.04 (Docker) Arch: amd64 (Intel i7-13700HX) &gt; Repository:<a href=\"http://packages.ros.org/ros2-testing/ubuntu\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://packages.ros.org/ros2-testing/ubuntu</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">ROS version or commit hash:</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">ROS 2 Lyrical Luth</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">RMW implementation (if applicable):</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">rmw_fastrtps_cpp</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">RMW Configuration (if applicable):</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Default</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Client library (if applicable):</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">insatllation issue</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">'ros2 doctor --report' output</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">\"Cannot run; installation failed to complete.\"</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Steps to reproduce issue</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">1.Start ubuntu:26.04 Docker container.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">2.Add ros2-testing repository.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">3.Run apt update.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">4.Run apt install ros-lyrical-desktop -y.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Expected behavior</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">he packages should download and install successfully</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Actual behavior</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">he process stopped at 99% with multiple '404 Not Found' errors for specific .deb files.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional information</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">am participating in the Lyrical Luth T&amp;T Party. I am testing on a Lenovo LOQ laptop using Docker. It appears the mirrors are not fully synced for the resolute (26.04) distribution.\"</p>",
